For missiles I will at least have a stack of blessed +5/6
elven daggers even for a class that can't enhance dagger
skill.  But classes that can use bow there's the launcher,
more than one type of arrow.  And any silver daggers ever
found.

For melee I don't hesitate to enchant early non-artifact
ones and build skills in assorted types.  The faster the
plan to ascend the less this makes sense but I generally
play endurance style (which says I'm less skilled, I get
that bit).  So I end up with 3-4 melee weapons +3 and
better by Medusa.

For artifacts I'll enchant Sunsword just because I might
want to use it in the swamp levels deep down.  For the
main chosen melee artifact like Exc/Grey/Storm/etc I
will be carrying it most of the game so it makes sense.
A class that can #twoweapon that ends up an artifact
and a non-artifact dual wielded.  A class that can't that
ends up two different types of artifact to "x" between.
Maybe Magicbane and Stormy, or Greyswandir and
Sunsword, or whatever happened to arrive in the game.

For the rest of artifacts I tend to enchant them because
the scrolls are there.  Style issue.


